WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.288 --> 00:00:16.190
carried Amy all the way home, talking to her, trying to keep her from falling asleep, because that

2
00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.451
would have lowered her body temperature even more.

3
00:00:19.571 --> 00:00:24.193
Jo was trying her best to contribute to the rescue mission but her whole body and mind were

4
00:00:24.273 --> 00:00:26.514
numb. "What if she dies?

5
00:00:26.874 --> 00:00:27.915
It'll be my fault.

6
00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.936
How can I live with myself if Amy dies?"

7
00:00:31.508 --> 00:00:33.910
Jo repeated over and over again under her breath.

8
00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.311
"She's not going to die, Jo.

9
00:00:36.752 --> 00:00:39.173
Just keep talking to her," Laurie panted.

10
00:00:40.134 --> 00:00:46.479
Even though his main concern was Amy, Laurie's thoughts never left his best friend, who he knew felt

11
00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.500
guilty about the unfortunate accident.

12
00:00:50.581 --> 00:00:51.262
"Mother March!"

13
00:00:51.602 --> 00:00:55.445
Laurie called out, kicking the door open with his foot when they got to the March home.

14
00:00:56.205 --> 00:00:58.607
Laurie was the only one who was allowed to call Mrs.

15
00:00:58.667 --> 00:00:59.668
March by that name.

16
00:01:00.504 --> 00:01:01.685
"Heavens! What's happened?"

17
00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:05.408
Mother gasped as soon as she saw the three of them burst into the house.

18
00:01:06.148 --> 00:01:10.631
Laying Amy in the chair closest to the fireplace, Laurie tried his best to explain.

19
00:01:11.312 --> 00:01:17.576
For some reason, seeing her Mother's pale-white face made Jo feel even guiltier and she could not control

20
00:01:17.596 --> 00:01:20.098
the tears that started to slide down her cheeks.

21
00:01:21.318 --> 00:01:23.460
Meanwhile, Mother was giving instructions to everyone.

22
00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:25.922
"Hannah! We need more wood.

23
00:01:26.282 --> 00:01:29.024
Meg, get some hot towels and boil a pot of hot water.

24
00:01:29.788 --> 00:01:33.771
Beth, go upstairs and grab every blanket you can find and bring them quickly.

25
00:01:34.171 --> 00:01:36.013
We need to keep her as warm as possible."

26
00:01:36.733 --> 00:01:39.775
Laurie stepped back, letting Mother take charge of the situation.

27
00:01:40.616 --> 00:01:43.678
He shivered, not realizing until then how cold he was.

28
00:01:44.659 --> 00:01:50.383
Warming himself by the fire, he glanced over at Jo, who was shaking visibly from the cold, but

29
00:01:50.423 --> 00:01:51.544
did not seem aware of it.

30
00:01:52.384 --> 00:01:56.968
Wordlessly, he went over to her, putting his arms around her shoulders and patting her gently.

31
00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:03.725
Jo, grateful for Laurie's kindness, leaned her head against him, and sobbed until no more tears would come

32
00:02:03.805 --> 00:02:09.349
out. With the exception of a slight numbness in her hands and feet, Amy was going to be

33
00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:15.755
fine. Laurie and Jo had acted speedily and saved Amy before any severe damage had happened.

34
00:02:16.415 --> 00:02:20.899
Still, Jo could not help but feel that Amy's fall was her fault in the first place.

35
00:02:20.919 --> 00:02:27.164
"Jo? Come here, dearest," Mother whispered when she saw Jo standing awkwardly at the doorway.

36
00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.323
Mother had just come in to check up on Amy, who was sleeping soundly.

37
00:02:32.144 --> 00:02:35.927
Jo paced outside the bedroom but did not have the courage to go inside.

38
00:02:36.688 --> 00:02:39.630
Her mother's kind words, though, seemed a warm invitation.

39
00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:41.712
"Amy is doing fine.

40
00:02:42.152 --> 00:02:44.935
She just needs to rest," Mother spoke softly.

41
00:02:45.455 --> 00:02:46.696
"You need some rest too."

42
00:02:47.857 --> 00:02:51.460
Jo felt her throat tighten and the tears sting her eyes once again.

43
00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:58.357
"Jo, whatever you are feeling, this was not your fault," Mother said, sensing Jo's painful guilt.

44
00:02:58.377 --> 00:03:00.658
"But it was.

45
00:03:01.518 --> 00:03:07.581
If I hadn't been so mean, she if only I hadn't lost my temper Jo choked.

46
00:03:09.342 --> 00:03:13.063
Mother pulled Jo close to her and whispered, "I understand how you feel."

47
00:03:13.083 --> 00:03:17.065
"How can you know what it feels like to be so angry, Mother?"

48
00:03:17.465 --> 00:03:18.025
sniffed Jo.

49
00:03:18.585 --> 00:03:21.687
"You're the most patient, kindest person in the world."

50
00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:29.187
Mother smiled shyly and said, "I try very hard but, to be honest, I used to be exactly

51
00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:29.827
like you."

52
00:03:31.008 --> 00:03:33.129
Jo stared at her mother unbelievingly.

53
00:03:33.909 --> 00:03:36.051
Mother was a role model for all her daughters.

54
00:03:37.191 --> 00:03:41.574
For her to admit that she had a temper like Jo's was too much of a shock.

55
00:03:42.274 --> 00:03:46.197
Shaking her head, Jo said, "No, I can't believe that, Mother.

56
00:03:46.657 --> 00:03:47.998
You're not like me at all."

57
00:03:49.619 --> 00:03:56.615
Chuckling quietly, Mother replied, "You may think I am perfect and make no mistakes but Jo, I'm also

58
00:03:56.695 --> 00:03:59.978
human. I have many faults and weaknesses.

59
00:04:00.778 --> 00:04:03.600
I'm just better able to control them as I get older."

60
00:04:04.421 --> 00:04:08.624
Jo, no longer crying, quietly contemplated her mother's words.

61
00:04:08.644 --> 00:04:12.126
"Do you think I will ever change and be like you?"

62
00:04:12.146 --> 00:04:16.049
"That depends on whether or not you want to change.

63
00:04:16.709 --> 00:04:20.192
Some people feel that anger makes them stronger and more respected.

64
00:04:21.104 --> 00:04:25.408
Others see that anger, though sometimes unavoidable, can be controlled.

65
00:04:26.128 --> 00:04:28.250
That is what I am learning," said Mother.

66
00:04:29.031 --> 00:04:31.653
Amy stirred and mumbled something softly in her sleep.

67
00:04:32.553 --> 00:04:37.918
Watching her, Jo confessed, "I thought I could never forgive her for destroying my story.

68
00:04:38.738 --> 00:04:40.380
I didn't want to forgive her."

69
00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.321
"How do you feel now?"

70
00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:43.642
Mother asked kindly.

71
00:04:43.662 --> 00:04:47.305
"I realize that I can always write another story.

72
00:04:48.186 --> 00:04:53.093
Amy might have ruined what I wrote down, but I still have it preserved in here."

73
00:04:53.694 --> 00:04:54.894
Jo tapped her heart.

74
00:04:54.914 --> 00:05:02.879
"And," she continued, "although stories may be replaceable, if I lost Amy, there would be no one to

75
00:05:02.939 --> 00:05:03.719
take her place."

76
00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:10.563
Mother gave Jo a kiss and patted her hand, saying, "Yes, you can and will change, Jo.

77
00:05:12.184 --> 00:05:15.246
One day, that temper of yours will no longer control you."

78
00:05:15.946 --> 00:05:19.048
Mother got up and left Jo to sit with Amy for a while.

79
00:05:20.128 --> 00:05:24.051
Jo started to feel better, knowing that perhaps she wasn't so hopeless.

80
00:05:24.071 --> 00:05:27.573
"If Mother can change, so can I.

81
00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:31.316
I am her daughter, after all," she said to herself.

82
00:05:31.336 --> 00:05:36.179
"Jo?" Amy whispered weakly, her eyes half-opened.

83
00:05:36.199 --> 00:05:40.102
"I'm here, darling," Jo replied warmly.

84
00:05:41.403 --> 00:05:43.905
Amy stared at her for a long time before speaking.

85
00:05:43.925 --> 00:05:46.647
"Jo? I'm so sorry.

86
00:05:47.227 --> 00:05:48.268
Please forgive me."

87
00:05:49.632 --> 00:05:55.014
Wiping her hand across her eyes, Jo, who had never cried so much in her life, took Amy's

88
00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.635
hand and held it close to her face.

89
00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:58.816
"Me, too, Amy.

90
00:05:59.636 --> 00:06:02.578
Let's forget all that's happened in the past and look forward.

91
00:06:03.098 --> 00:06:03.878
What do you say?"

92
00:06:05.139 --> 00:06:09.761
Amy gave Jo a faint smile and squeezed her hand as she answered, "Thank you, Jo."

93
00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:13.442
That evening, Jo could not sleep.

94
00:06:14.162 --> 00:06:17.464
Her mind was racing with thoughts about the events of the past few days.

95
00:06:18.356 --> 00:06:23.641
She suddenly found herself wanting to put everything down in writing because a story was forming in her

96
00:06:23.681 --> 00:06:29.746
head. When the other girls had gone to sleep, Jo crept up to her sanctuary, a place she

97
00:06:29.766 --> 00:06:34.730
had not visited since Amy had destroyed her story, and sat at the old familiar desk.

98
00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:40.895
She began to write, her pen flying over the paper, while she tried to jot down every word

99
00:06:40.955 --> 00:06:41.676
spilling out of her.

100
00:06:42.836 --> 00:06:45.479
In the end, Jo stayed up all night completing her story.

101
00:06:46.299 --> 00:06:52.491
Finally, Jo leaned back in her chair and, stretching her neck and shoulders, thought of the perfect title

102
00:06:52.571 --> 00:06:53.251
for her story.

103
00:06:54.252 --> 00:07:01.015
Taking a clean sheet of paper, she wrote in big letters "Like Mother, Like Daughter—A story by Josephine

104
00:07:01.056 --> 00:07:07.399
March." Cradling her chin in her hand, Jo watched the sun rise, glad to be alive and to

105
00:07:07.459 --> 00:07:09.200
enjoy another beautiful day.
